# CAPTURE OWNERSHIP — a closure captures a collection and the SOURCE is then
# reallocated out from under it. The environment holds its own value, so the
# realloc cannot reach it.
#
#     Callable[String()] f = (): v.get(0).unwrap()   # captures `v`
#     while i < 64: v.push(mk(…))                    # `v` reallocates
#     print(f())                                     # still `hello`
#
# THE RULE THIS PINS. A closure capture is an ownership boundary, so it obeys
# the same table every other consuming position obeys: clone if the source is
# still live, move if it is dead. `v` is live across 64 pushes, so the capture
# clones, and the environment's field is an independent collection that no
# realloc of `v` can sever.
#
# ⚠ THE REALLOC IS LOAD-BEARING (64 pushes, not one) and the payload must be
# heap-FORCED through `mk`, never a literal: a string literal is `.rodata` with
# `cap = 0` and `gorget_string_free` no-ops on it, so a literal payload proves
# nothing. 0 pushes and 1 push are both rc 0 without the rule.
#
# ⚠ THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE CAPTURE ROOT, NOT WHERE THE MUTATION IS SPELLED.
# The sibling `closure_capture_inside_body_uaf.gg` reallocates INSIDE the body
# with no saved view variable at all; `cow_closure_body_view_survives_realloc.gg`
# runs the identical statements with the vector LOCAL to the closure — no
# capture, and it was already correct. Capture is what makes this shape a
# boundary.
#
# ⚠ THE INSTRUMENT IS C + ASan. Without the rule this is rc 139 on both
# backends, and under `--backend=llvm --sanitize` the aggregate sibling reports
# only a leak (`todo/t0731`).
#
# Prints `hello`, both backends, ASan-clean.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    String() f = (): v.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        v.push(mk("fill", "er"))
        i = i + 1
    print(f())
